  {
    "id": "686d5916f9ac2b19628e2787",
    "title": "Employee Spotlight: Simon Smucker",
    "slug": "employee-spotlight-simon-smucker",
    "excerpt": "...",
    "content": "CAPS is pleased to welcome Simon Smucker as the new Chief Financial Officer. Simon says he accepted the position because “I wanted to work at an organization where I care about the mission and what’s happening – to be able to do what I like to do and have it be helpful towards an end goal beyond the bottom line. CAPS is a good fit.”\n\nSimon started his career as an accountant at Kruggel Lawton doing audit and tax work, primarily for nonprofit clients. After three years at the firm, Simon and his wife Becca moved to Bolivia to serve with Mennonite Central Committee, an organization that does national and international peace and development work. “We both had an interest in doing long-term service and building relationships in another culture.” During their time in Bolivia, Simon managed the accounting for the organization and Becca facilitated a young adult exchange program.\n\n“I had to learn how to do my job in a whole new context. In Bolivia, the financial reporting and local fiscal rules are very different. Becca supported the young adult volunteers with adaptation challenges – culture shock, living with a host family, and conflict resolution. We were making our own adjustments to language, transportation, and climate differences…we learned a lot in the three years we spent there. It was a time of meaningful personal growth.”\n\nWhen their time in Bolivia drew to a close, they returned to the US and moved to Cleveland, Ohio where Becca completed her MSW at Case Western Reserve University. Simon took a position as the Controller at a nonprofit organization that provided mental health and crisis services. Simon was excited when the CFO position opened at CAPS and it felt like good timing, since Simon and Becca are expecting their first baby in July and wanted to return to Goshen to be near family.\n\nSo what is Simon’s reaction to a new job, moving and a new baby? “Lots of changes, but they’re all good!” he says with a smile.\n\nFor job opportunities at CAPS, visit our Career Page.",
    "published": "2021-07-20T04:01:46Z",
    "image": "",
    "featured": false,
    "category": "686d59126b8307c8dfdcde48",
    "tags": "[]"
  },
  {
    "id": "686d592cf04dc635589af1b6",
    "title": "Veteran CFO and CAPS Board Member Appointed as New CFO",
    "slug": "veteran-cfo-and-caps-board-member-appointed-as-new-cfo",
    "excerpt": "...",
    "content": "We’re thrilled to announce that Brian Hall has officially joined CAPS as our new Chief Financial Officer (CFO). Brian brings more than just an impressive resume; he brings a passion for our mission and a deep understanding of CAPS that stretches back over two decades. A Bit About Brian Brian’s professional journey began in Warsaw, Indiana , where he was born and raised. After earning his degree in accounting from Indiana University , he dedicated 17 years to public accounting before spending the last decade as CFO of Lippert . Throughout his career, Brian has been a trusted financial leader, consistently bringing stability and growth to the organizations he’s served. But it’s not just Brian’s financial expertise that makes him the right fit for this role. His over 20 years of involvement with CAPS as a Board member have given him invaluable insight into our mission and operations. Having worked closely with every CAPS CEO since Daryll Abbott, Brian has gained a deep understanding of how we function and the impact we strive to make. A Personal Connection to Our Mission What sets Brian apart isn’t just his career success, it’s his passion  for CAPS and what we stand for. Over the years, Brian has committed his time and energy to serving on various committees, helping steer the direction of CAPS and advocating for the children and families we serve. “I’ve always had a passion for what CAPS stands for,” Brian shared recently. “After nearly twenty years of board and committee service with CAPS, it is such an honor and privilege to join the incredible CAPS staff as a member of their team. While board work is incredibly important, it always left me with a feeling of not doing enough. Now I get a chance to remedy that.” Brian’s Vision for CAPS As CFO, Brian is eager to leverage his experience  to strengthen CAPS’ financial health and ensure we can continue to grow our impact in the community. He’s focused on exploring new opportunities while maintaining the solid foundation that’s been built over the years. “I'm looking forward to working alongside the amazing team here at CAPS,” Brian said. “Together, we’ll continue to fulfill the CAPS mission and ensure that every child has the opportunity to thrive in a safe and supportive environment.” Looking Forward With Brian on board, we’re excited for the future. His leadership  and expertise will undoubtedly help CAPS grow and continue to make a difference in the lives of children and families.",
