  {
    "id": "686d5935f04dc635589af1e1",
    "title": "Volunteer Highlight: Lyndsay Hemmick",
    "slug": "volunteer-highlight-lyndsay-hemmick",
    "excerpt": "Volunteer highligh: Lyndsay Hemmick",
    "content": "Elkhart native and dedicated CAPS board member, Lyndsay McBride Hemmick, brings a unique blend of creativity and commitment to her role, balancing a career in finance with a deep love for art and design. Lyndsay and her husband, Aaron, are proud parents to three children. They are also licensed foster and adoptive parents, reflecting their strong dedication to family and community. As co-chair of the CAPS Gala Task Force Team, Lyndsay plays an essential role in shaping one of the organization’s most important annual events. She helps lead the effort in establishing the gala’s theme, coordinating monthly meetings, and making key decisions on everything from floral arrangements and place settings to invitations and the evening's happenings. An artist at heart, Lyndsay also donates her own artwork to the CAPS silent art auction, a highlight of the gala that celebrates local talent while supporting a meaningful cause. We are incredibly grateful for Lyndsay’s dedication to CAPS and her tireless work on the Gala Task Force. Her creativity, passion, and thoughtful leadership help bring the event to life in inspiring ways. Her commitment ensures the the event raises support to fund CAPS' programs, making a lasting impact on our mission and the community we serve. “Being part of CAPS allows me to pour my heart into something that truly matters,” says Lyndsay. “I love combining my passion for art and design with a cause that supports children and families. It’s an honor to play a role in creating an event that brings people together for such an important purpose.",
